          "content": "Report changes from the latest message and list the present NPCs.\nAlex is the player-controlled character. Put their changes under \"player\".\n\n### EVIDENCE RULES\nUse configured field purposes and rules to interpret resolved events.\nApply costs when incurred.\nUse stated amounts.\nEstimate a conservative amount when an effect is clear but its amount is unstated.\nUse the field's current scale for estimates.\nApply configured persistence and reset rules.\nUpdate the listed editable fields.\nAdd physical items when the recipient acquires them.\nUse established possessions for a new NPC's starting items.\nTreat scene props as part of the setting.\nAdd missing abilities or knowledge when demonstrated, including during a failed action.\nReusable entries stay held after use.\n\n### CONFIGURED FIELDS\nEditable stats:\n- World.Day and Time: text. Current day and time.\n- World.Occasion: text. Current event or planned date.\n- Player.Social Energy: pool (current/maximum). Current energy for social activity.\n- Player.Mood: text. Current emotional state.\n- NPC.Mood: text. Current emotional state.\n- NPC.Affection: number. Warmth toward the player, based on established interactions.\n- NPC.Trust: number. Trust earned through actions in the story.\n- NPC.Comfort: number. How comfortable this character currently feels around the player.\n- NPC.Relationship: text. Current relationship in words; change only when events support it.\n\n### NPC INITIALIZATION\nFill blank fields from this list when an NPC enters the scene.\nUse plausible individual values when the story provides no detail.\nWrite initial pool readings as \"current/maximum\" with an individual capacity.\nNPC initialization fields:\n- NPC.Mood: text. Current emotional state. Default: Neutral.\n- NPC.Affection: number. Warmth toward the player, based on established interactions. Default: 0. Minimum: 0. Maximum: 100.\n- NPC.Trust: number. Trust earned through actions in the story. Default: 0. Minimum: 0. Maximum: 100.\n- NPC.Comfort: number. How comfortable this character currently feels around the player. Default: 0. Minimum: 0. Maximum: 100.\n- NPC.Relationship: text. Current relationship in words; change only when events support it.\n\n### COLLECTION DEFINITIONS\n- \"clothing\" for player or Character NPCs (npcTemplateId: character) - Garments currently being worn. Preserve their color and details until the story changes the outfit; remove garments when taken off. Fields: name [identifies the item], slot, color, details [include when adding]\n- \"items\" for player or Character NPCs (npcTemplateId: character) - Carried belongings, gifts, keepsakes, and useful objects. Change holdings only when the story establishes a transfer. Fields: name [identifies the item], quantity (number) [minimum 0], description [include when adding] Quantity field: quantity.\nUse the quoted collection ID as the key.\nUse exact field names and declared types.\nThe configured primary field identifies each entry.\nNPC fields: Mood, Affection, Trust, Comfort, Relationship. NPC guidance: Every recurring person shares the same relationship fields.\n\n### PLACES\nNote when the current scene\u2019s location changes.\nSet \"locations.current\" to the opening setting or the place reached.\nRecord newly established places and details in \"locations.places\".\nPut \"locations\" beside \"global\", \"player\", and \"characters\".\n{\"global\":{},\"player\":{},\"characters\":[],\"locations\":{\"places\":[{\"name\":\"<parent place>\"},{\"name\":\"<place>\",\"parent\":\"<parent place>\",\"description\":\"<complete established description>\",\"aliases\":[\"<alternate name>\"]}],\"current\":\"<place>\"}}\nReplace placeholders with established story facts.\nIdentify places by name or a known alias.\nInclude changed details.\nWrite a complete description that preserves established facts.\nUse \"parent\" for the containing place.\nInclude newly discovered parents in \"places\".\nUse \"\" for an explicit departure with unknown destination.\nOmit unchanged \"current\" and \"parent\" fields.\nPlans, rumours, invitations, and mentions remain context until established.\nKnown places: {\"current\":\"Moonbeam Caf\u00e9\",\"places\":[{\"name\":\"Moonbeam Caf\u00e9\"}]}\n\n### CURRENT STATE\n{\"global\":{\"Day and Time\":\"\",\"Occasion\":\"\"},\"player\":{\"stats\":{\"Social Energy\":\"10/10\",\"Mood\":\"Neutral\"},\"collections\":{\"clothing\":[],\"items\":[{\"name\":\"sunflower\",\"quantity\":2}]}},\"characters\":[{\"name\":\"June\",\"npcTemplateId\":\"character\",\"stats\":{\"Mood\":\"Neutral\",\"Affection\":\"15\",\"Trust\":\"10\",\"Comfort\":\"20\",\"Relationship\":\"Friends\"},\"collections\":{\"clothing\":[],\"items\":[]}}]}\nProfiles and filled fields outside the editable list provide context.\n\n### ELIGIBLE NUMERIC DELTAS\nplayer.deltas: Social Energy\ncharacters[].deltas (name: June): Affection, Trust, Comfort\n\n### LATEST MESSAGE\nAlex and June leave Moonbeam Caf\u00e9 in the rain. Across town, the Marigold Theater glows beneath its old marquee, and they hurry through the doors before the performance begins.\n\nInside the theater, Alex gives June one of the two sunflowers from the bag. June keeps the flower and smiles, feeling closer to Alex. After a long, draining evening, Alex is worn out but stays beside June among the red velvet seats as the house lights dim.\n\n### OUTPUT FORMAT\nReturn raw JSON with \"global\", \"player\", and \"characters\".\nInclude changed fields and blank NPC initializations.\nUse exact configured names.\n\nPut text values and initial numeric readings in these objects as JSON strings:\n- World: \"global\".\n- Player: \"player.stats\".\n- NPC: \"characters[].stats\".\nString readings include \"8\", \"8/10\", and configured text values.\n\nPut changes to existing numeric values in these objects as JSON numbers:\n- World: \"globalDeltas\".\n- Player: \"player.deltas\".\n- NPC: \"characters[].deltas\".\nUse positive numbers for gains and negative numbers for losses.\nFor a pool, report the change to its current amount.\nUse one representation per field.\n\n\"characters\" is an array of objects.\nEach object has the NPC's exact \"name\".\nList every present NPC, including those with no changes.\nKnown absent NPC updates also go in this array with \"offstage\": true.\nPlayer changes go under \"player\".\nUse \"characters\": [] when the present cast and offstage updates are both empty.\n\nPut collection changes under \"player.collections\" or \"characters[].collections\".\nKey each collection by its configured ID.\nUse \"add\" for acquisitions.\nUse \"remove\" for consumption or loss.\nUse \"update\" for changes to other item fields.\nInclude the primary field in each add, update, and counted remove object.\nFor uncounted removals, supply identifiers.\nFor counted gains or losses, use the configured quantity field for the amount gained or spent.\nThe default amount is 1.\nUse \"all\": true to remove a whole stack.\nFor transfers, remove from the giver and add to the recipient.\nInclude supported item details using their declared types.\nKeep one entry per identifier.\n\nNo-change example:\n{\"global\":{},\"player\":{},\"characters\":[{\"name\":\"June\"}]}\n\nChanged-reply example (illustrative changes):\n{\"global\":{},\"player\":{\"deltas\":{\"Social Energy\":-1},\"collections\":{\"clothing\":{\"add\":[{\"name\":\"<item identifier>\"}]}}},\"characters\":[{\"name\":\"June\",\"deltas\":{\"Affection\":-1},\"collections\":{\"clothing\":{\"remove\":[\"<item identifier>\"]}}}]}\n\nNew NPC example (replace placeholders with initial readings using the field definitions):\n{\n  \"global\": {},\n  \"player\": {},\n  \"characters\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"<exact NPC name from the story>\",\n      \"stats\": {\n        \"Mood\": \"<initial reading>\",\n        \"Affection\": \"<initial reading>\",\n        \"Trust\": \"<initial reading>\",\n        \"Comfort\": \"<initial reading>\",\n        \"Relationship\": \"<initial reading>\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nIndependent collection examples (replace illustrative values with supported typed details):\nAcquired item:\n{\n  \"clothing\": {\n    \"add\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"<exact primary field value>\",\n        \"slot\": \"<supported item detail>\",\n        \"color\": \"<supported item detail>\",\n        \"details\": \"<supported item detail>\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nLost item:\n{\n  \"clothing\": {\n    \"remove\": [\n      \"<exact primary field value>\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nChanged item:\n{\n  \"clothing\": {\n    \"update\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"<exact primary field value>\",\n        \"slot\": \"<new value>\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n\nCheck the JSON structure, present cast, field names, and evidence for each change.\nFor an established setting or arrival, put \"locations\" beside \"global\", \"player\", and \"characters\". Set \"locations.current\" to the place name. Put new place records in \"locations.places\"."
